    "final_answer": "For a centrifugal pump, the available net positive suction head (NPSHA) must be equal to or greater than the required net positive suction head (NPSHR). [KB1]\nIf NPSHA is less than NPSHR, cavitation or flashing may occur in the pump suction. [KB1]\nNPSH is defined as the total suction head in feet of liquid (absolute at the pump centerline or impeller eye) less the vapor pressure (in feet) of the liquid being pumped. [KB3]\nThe total dynamic head (TDH) required of a pump is the difference between the suction and discharge heads. [KB3]",
